[ti:Day 12]

[00:00.00]terminate 例 There must be some reason to terminate an employee in our company. 在我们公司，不 能无故解雇员工。
[00:09.88]gadget 例 This week on the gadget show, we found out what the best printers on the market are. 在本周的小器具展上，我们发现了市场上最好的 打印机。
[00:21.29]amateur 例 The mark of the amateur in any field is to lose one's head when the going gets hard. 无 论在哪一领域，生手的标志就是在困难面前惊慌 失措。
[00:32.70]array 例 Trade was restricted by an array of taxes and prohibitions on imports and exports. 贸易 受到一系列进出口税和禁令的限制。
[00:44.10]breadwinner 例 Nowadays, more women take on the role of breadwinner. 如今越来越多的妇女承担起养家糊 口的角色。
[00:52.77]pledge 例 The contract pledges the two companies to cooperate with each other. 合约保证这两家公 司将进行合作。
[01:02.66]equilibrium 例 In simple words, when supply equates demand, we get an equilibrium. 简而言之，当 市场供求一样的时候，就达到了一个平衡点。
[01:13.15]emit 例 He emitted his proposal to the functional draft. 他表达了对功能草案的提议。
[01:20.15]maximise 例 The CFO of the company should measure the outcomes to maximise their profit. 公司的 首席财务官应权衡结果，以使利润最大化。
[01:31.25]aviation 例 The Association of Southeast Asian Nations is working on establishing a single aviation market with no traffic restrictions by 2015. 东 南亚国家联盟正努力在2015年之前建立起一个单 一的、没有交通限制的航空市场。
[01:49.81]ladder 例 Many computers used the binary system in the past. 过去，许多电子计算机都使用二进制系 统。
[01:57.26]undo 例 The climbing price of crude oil might undo America's economic recovery. 原油价格的攀升 可能会破坏美国的经济复苏。
[02:07.30]cereal 例 As corn prices rise, some ranchers are choosing wheat as a feed crop, boosting demand for the cereal and its price. 由于玉米 价格上涨，一些牧场主选择小麦作为饲料作物， 提升了这种谷物的需求及其价格。
[02:22.81]bespoke 例 The bespoke furniture for our new house is very appropriate. 为我们的新房定做的家具非常 合适。
[02:31.78]scope 例 They scoped out the local market before starting the business. 在做这个生意之前，他们 已经对当地市场作了评估。
[02:40.75]hook 例 Music is often the hook to the visuals. 音乐 经常能够成为增强视觉效果的手段。
[02:46.38]ceremony 例 This ceremony has a special meaning for all of us. 此次仪式对于我们所有人都有特殊意 义。
[02:53.99]boom 例 The government needs to keep a watchful eye on the investment boom risk. 政府需要密切 关注投资激增风险。
[03:03.87]consecutive 例 Two consecutive tasks in a business model may use different business items as the output and input. 业务模型中的两个连续任务可 以将不同的业务项目用做输出和输入。
[03:18.32]annualised 例 In order to borrow the shares, the investors have to pay the owner an annualised percentage of the stock's value. 为借入股票， 投资者要向股票所有人支付股票价值的年利率。
[03:34.29]fiat 例 The urban population grows by administrative fiat, not by the actual move of the population from the country to the city. 城 市人口的增长是通过行政命令而非人口从乡村到 城市的实际迁徙实现的。
[03:50.41]unwind 例 The picnic will give you a chance to unwind. 这次野餐会给你一次放松的机会。
[03:56.95]dip 例 We dipped into our savings. 我们动用了存 款。
[04:01.06]high-tech 例 The demands for the simplicity of high- tech products are increasing as the economy is in the upswing. 随着经济的蓬勃发展，人们对 高科技产品简洁性的需求也在增长。
[04:15.51]broadband 例 This was an important company since it started the broadband revolution that eventually spread around the world. 这是一家 很重要的公司，因为它曾掀起最终波及全世界的 宽带革命。
[04:31.63]reinstall 例 Through negotiation, the employer agreed to reinstall the former personnel manager. 经 过商议，老板同意重新起用前人事经理。
[04:44.25]appropriate 例 You can then select the appropriate product from this full list. 你可以从这个完整的 列表中选择适当的产品。
[04:54.29]fuss 例 There will be a fuss when the media get hold of the story. 媒介得知此事后会小题大做。
[05:02.05]upswing 例 Tourism in China has witnessed a dramatic upswing in recent years. 近年来，中国的旅游业 发展极快。
[05:11.78]disrupt 例 Will these emerging giants disrupt the framework for sustainable development? 这些 新兴大国会瓦解可持续发展架构吗？
[05:23.34]documentary 例 A documentary draft can offer greater security to the exporter. 跟单汇票对出口商来说 会更为保险。
[05:33.38]overqualified 例 You are overqualified for this kind of job. 对 于这种工作而言，你资历过高了。
[05:40.98]jet-setter 例 Many jet-setters attended the party held by the billionaire. 许多名流都参加了那位亿万富翁 举办的聚会。
[05:50.56]patience 例 Like it or not, the work does require some time and patience. 无论你喜欢与否，这项工作 确实需要一些时间和耐心。
[05:59.54]realign 例 Our company will realign its global resources next month. 下个月，我们公司将对所 拥有的全球资源进行重新调整。
[06:08.21]stem 例 Many bankers expressed worry over the risks that stem from lending to the property sector. 许多银行家都表示出对于房地产领域的借 贷风险的担心。
[06:20.52]bureaucracy 例 Bureaucracy shouldn't occur in our company. 官僚作风不应该出现在我们公司。
[06:28.13]ballot 例 The result of the ballot will not be declared to the public until this weekend. 这个周末将会 向公众宣布投票结果。
[06:39.08]navigate 例 Because of the complicated traffic system in the city, I determined to set up GPS in the car for navigating destinations. 鉴于这座城市复 杂的交通系统，我决定在车上安装GPS用于导 航。
[06:55.81]mastermind 例 He is the well-recognised mastermind of the department. 他是这个部门公认的才子。
[07:04.78]field 例 They will also scope out another new field. 他们还将开拓另一个新的领域。
[07:11.17]civil 例 Debates about war and peace as well as those about security and civil liberties have often been fierce. 有关战争与和平、安全与公民 自由的讨论常常是激烈的。
[07:25.16]delegate 例 All delegates attending the two sessions should value their opportunities to speak for people. 参加两会的所有代表都应该珍惜他们为人 民说话的机会。
[07:38.85]gratis 例 The salesman told us the samples were sent gratis. 售货员告诉我们那些样品是免费赠送 的。
[07:46.30]counteroffer 例 If you cannot accept our offer, please make the best possible counteroffer. 如果你方不能接 受我们的报价，请给出最有可能的还盘。
[07:58.01]sacred 例 The foreign supplier offered us many favourable terms, even allowing the payment 30 days after sight. 那家国外供货商给我们提供 了很多优惠条件，甚至允许我们见票30天后付 款。
[08:12.16]snap 例 Please make a snap decision about what you want to buy. 请快速决定您要买什么。 paid leave 带薪假期 例 Every employee in the company is entitled to an annual paid leave of ten days. 该公司的 员工每年都拥有10天的带薪假期。
[08:19.76]localise 例 Some international companies are making efforts to localise their operations. 一些跨国公 司正努力推动经营的本土化。
[08:31.47]finding 例 They recently published the findings of a study on this topic. 最近他们发布了有关这个专 题的调查结果。
[08:40.60]encrypt 例 We plan to buy the software to encrypt our products. 我们打算买下那款软件，为我们的产品 加密。
[08:48.35]deposit 例 At present, the turnover tax of banks in China is levied according to the margin between the borrowing rate and deposit rate. 目前，中国的银行营业税是依据借款汇率和存款 汇率的差额来征收的。
[09:05.39]thrust 例 All of these jobs are thrust on her. 所有这些 工作都是强加给她的。
[09:10.86]majority 例 The majority of these employees have no voice. 这些员工中的绝大多数人都没有发言权。
[09:18.16]reprobate 例 She was determined to reprobate such a common system. 她决定摈弃这种常用的系统。
[09:26.53]cohesion 例 More worrying is what all this tells us about the fundamental cohesion of the Union. 更令人 担心的是，上述这一切告诉我们，欧盟的根本凝 聚力出现了问题。
[09:38.54]naval 例 As an important naval base, the harbour has got great attention from the local government. 作为重要的海军基地，该港口受到 当地政府的高度重视。
